CloudBurrow patch 7 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1061; the bugs: #1107, #1123).

The bug: with a default dataset, a call of another dataset's SQL function,
`SELECT one.fn(1)` with the default dataset `two`, failed "no such column:
<project>". The analyzer resolved the call to the right function (it is
registered under every suffix of its path), but Analyzer.Analyze built the
map of SQL functions (and table functions) it inlines from the connection's
name path only: Catalog.getFunctions kept a function only when the
default dataset's "project_dataset" key was a substring of the function's
own prefix. The formatter then wrote the call as the function's bare
storage name, `proj_one_fn(1)`, which SQLite read as columns. It failed so
in a query, a script and DDL (CREATE TABLE AS SELECT, CREATE VIEW), and for
a table function of another dataset ("TVF spec not found"). The patch
collects every function and table function of the catalog: the maps are
keyed by each function's full storage name, which is what a resolved call
names, so no other call changes. function_of_another_dataset_test.go fails
without the patch and passes with it.

